1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,208
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:12,875 --> 00:00:13,875
H'yah!

3
00:00:13,875 --> 00:00:14,958
[shattering]

4
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:18,666
[stamping]

5
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:19,750
[wind whooshing]

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:23,208
And I can expect
the remaining two chains

7
00:00:23,208 --> 00:00:25,958
to be eliminated... when?

8
00:00:25,958 --> 00:00:28,208
The final Prismatic Blades

9
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:31,333
are being hunted down
as we speak.

10
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:34,000
They'd better be.

11
00:00:36,541 --> 00:00:39,625
So the Merge created
new monasteries in each realm?

12
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:41,208
That is my theory,

13
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:43,041
but there is so much
about the Merge

14
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:44,500
we still do not understand.

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,166
The idea
of traveling to realms

16
00:00:46,166 --> 00:00:49,750
once nearly impossible to reach
is... invigorating.

17
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:52,375
I am surprised
you have not gone exploring.

18
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:54,791
As much as I enjoy
learning new things,

19
00:00:54,791 --> 00:00:57,583
I enjoy them more
when I share them with you,

20
00:00:57,583 --> 00:00:59,583
and you were not here.

21
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:01,791
I am here now.

22
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:07,125
We're, uh, not trying
to interrupt--

23
00:01:07,125 --> 00:01:09,583
Oh, yes. Uh, of course.

24
00:01:09,583 --> 00:01:10,750
Ninjago.

25
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:18,291
Nya! Kai!

26
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:19,583
So glad you're here!

27
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,250
Where's Wyldfyre?

28
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,791
Roby's not getting any better,

29
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:23,791
so she's staying back in--

30
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:24,791
[gasping]

31
00:01:24,791 --> 00:01:25,916
Pixal?!

32
00:01:25,916 --> 00:01:27,791
I can't believe it!

33
00:01:27,791 --> 00:01:29,833
A pleasure
to see you again, Nya.

34
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,833
I am told
it has been some time.

35
00:01:32,791 --> 00:01:35,041
Zane... you're...

36
00:01:35,041 --> 00:01:36,041
huge.

37
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:37,958
I got swole for buffness.

38
00:01:37,958 --> 00:01:39,500
[laughing] What?

39
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:40,625
A joke.

40
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:42,916
Nindroids do not build muscles
in that way.

41
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:44,333
Hence the humor.

42
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:45,791
Amusing!

43
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:48,875
Sora about told us
about the Forbidden Five

44
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:51,875
trying to unleash
some... big ancient dragon?

45
00:01:51,875 --> 00:01:54,125
The Shatter Dragon of Chaos.

46
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:56,500
They need five
specific Prismatic Blades

47
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,833
to cut the dragon's
enchanted chains,

48
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,958
one blade for each chain.

49
00:02:00,958 --> 00:02:02,875
They already have
three of them.

50
00:02:02,875 --> 00:02:05,666
Then good thing
we've got this one.

51
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:08,833
If they need all the blades,
just destroy it.

52
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:09,750
Problem solved.

53
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:11,416
Just call me "the Solver."

54
00:02:11,416 --> 00:02:14,208
One of them did shatter
in the tournament.

55
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:15,583
So maybe...

56
00:02:17,583 --> 00:02:18,791
[sighing]

57
00:02:18,791 --> 00:02:21,541
Let the Solver solve this.

58
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,833
So maybe the blade breaking
at the tournament

59
00:02:29,833 --> 00:02:32,041
was some special situation?

60
00:02:32,041 --> 00:02:34,041
Maybe magical?

61
00:02:34,041 --> 00:02:36,500
The Dragonians can sense
where the blades are.

62
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,000
The Monastery is in danger.

63
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,125
Then let's take it with us

64
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:41,916
to find the last missing blade.

65
00:02:41,916 --> 00:02:43,000
How do we find it?

66
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,666
We don't have
Dragonian trackers.

67
00:02:44,666 --> 00:02:47,583
Huh, the Solver has no solve?

68
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:48,583
I...

69
00:02:48,583 --> 00:02:50,166
[groaning] deserve that.

70
00:02:55,291 --> 00:02:56,458
I believe Zane and I

71
00:02:56,458 --> 00:02:59,916
can find a way
to track down the final blade.

72
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:06,041
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

73
00:03:06,041 --> 00:03:08,916
♪ Together we will rise ♪

74
00:03:08,916 --> 00:03:12,375
♪ We fight ♪

75
00:03:12,375 --> 00:03:15,458
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

76
00:03:17,708 --> 00:03:19,958
[♪♪♪]

77
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:32,458
Roby!

78
00:03:32,458 --> 00:03:34,333
Looking so much better!

79
00:03:37,375 --> 00:03:39,750
He's looking so much worse!

80
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:40,875
Where are we on a cure?

81
00:03:40,875 --> 00:03:42,833
No solution
has been identified

82
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:44,541
in any of our Books of Lore.

83
00:03:44,541 --> 00:03:45,416
[groaning]

84
00:03:45,416 --> 00:03:47,458
Books of Lore are the worst!

85
00:03:48,791 --> 00:03:52,291
Got it! Janus Melon Stew!

86
00:03:52,291 --> 00:03:54,291
Roby is not suffering
from hunger.

87
00:03:54,291 --> 00:03:57,166
The stew helps dragons
with the Wasting Sickness.

88
00:03:57,166 --> 00:03:58,750
If it'll help big dragons,

89
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:01,500
imagine what it'll do
for tiny people...

90
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,041
maybe cure anything!

91
00:04:03,041 --> 00:04:04,416
That logic is--

92
00:04:04,416 --> 00:04:05,500
Perfect, I know.

93
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,833
Where can I get Janus Melons
around here?

94
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:09,208
They are rare,

95
00:04:09,208 --> 00:04:12,875
but have been seen at the end
of the Jagged Tunnels,

96
00:04:12,875 --> 00:04:16,708
an underground path
of almost always fatal dangers.

97
00:04:16,708 --> 00:04:19,666
Cool. I'm gonna pop over there.

98
00:04:19,666 --> 00:04:22,291
Your chances
of total destruction there

99
00:04:22,291 --> 00:04:23,333
are near certain.

100
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:24,583
Nah. I'm good.

101
00:04:24,583 --> 00:04:26,000
Can I borrow a ride, though?

102
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,541
You may use any vehicle
in the City's fleet.

103
00:04:28,541 --> 00:04:29,541
Noice!

104
00:04:29,541 --> 00:04:31,750
Something with racing stripes?

105
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,916
Kai taught me
all about racing stripes.

106
00:04:33,916 --> 00:04:35,583
They make things go faster.

107
00:04:35,583 --> 00:04:38,250
It is as if
you cannot hear my warning

108
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:39,791
about your impending destruction

109
00:04:39,791 --> 00:04:41,833
if you pursue
this course of action.

110
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:42,750
My guy,

111
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,125
for Roby, I'd face, like,

112
00:04:44,125 --> 00:04:46,416
a million
impending destructions.

113
00:04:46,416 --> 00:04:48,666
Now, point me at something
that goes fast!

114
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:57,375
Do you remember
the exact location

115
00:04:57,375 --> 00:05:00,166
of the Temple
of the Dragon Cores?

116
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:02,000
Of course.

117
00:05:03,375 --> 00:05:05,458
I sense you are distracted.

118
00:05:05,458 --> 00:05:06,458
No...

119
00:05:06,458 --> 00:05:08,250
Well, my parents.

120
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:09,666
That cemetery.

121
00:05:09,666 --> 00:05:11,500
How'd you know it was there?

122
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:12,875
I told you.

123
00:05:12,875 --> 00:05:14,791
Everything Jay Walker learned

124
00:05:14,791 --> 00:05:16,750
from his time
in the Administration

125
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,916
is now known by me.

126
00:05:18,916 --> 00:05:21,250
And you'll really be able
to do what you said?

127
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:22,333
Bring them back?

128
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:23,750
Undoing the Merge

129
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:24,958
will release powers

130
00:05:24,958 --> 00:05:27,250
more potent than anything
seen in these realms

131
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:28,750
since their creation...

132
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:32,000
the ability
to reshape reality itself.

133
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,666
Do you doubt me?

134
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:36,416
No, but I have
so many questions

135
00:05:36,416 --> 00:05:37,750
about my parents.

136
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:39,958
During all those MergeQuakes
over the Crossroads,

137
00:05:39,958 --> 00:05:41,583
I swear I saw--

138
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:45,250
What was that?

139
00:05:46,375 --> 00:05:47,291
There.

140
00:05:50,666 --> 00:05:52,291
[Arin] Friend of yours?

141
00:05:52,291 --> 00:05:53,666
An unknown enemy.

142
00:05:53,666 --> 00:05:55,958
Just because they're unknown
doesn't make them an enemy.

143
00:05:55,958 --> 00:05:57,916
The unknown
is always the enemy.

144
00:05:57,916 --> 00:05:59,333
Whoa, Mr. Cynical.

145
00:05:59,333 --> 00:06:01,833
The unknown is usually
a potential friend.

146
00:06:03,416 --> 00:06:04,916
Where'd he go?

147
00:06:06,541 --> 00:06:08,291
[explosion]

148
00:06:08,291 --> 00:06:09,916
[alerts beeping]

149
00:06:12,958 --> 00:06:16,875
Our potential friend
is bombing us.

150
00:06:16,875 --> 00:06:18,458
-[grunting]
-[yelping]

151
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,500
[explosion]

152
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,791
Yeah, okay, not a friend!

153
00:06:24,291 --> 00:06:25,291
[explosions]

154
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:34,541
[grunting and groaning]

155
00:06:37,083 --> 00:06:38,250
[blasting]

156
00:06:45,875 --> 00:06:46,833
Ah!

157
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:47,958
[gasping]

158
00:06:49,041 --> 00:06:52,375
So you seriously
have no idea who this is?

159
00:06:52,375 --> 00:06:53,208
No.

160
00:06:53,208 --> 00:06:54,416
And it doesn't bother you

161
00:06:54,416 --> 00:06:56,541
that random people
just want to take you down?

162
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:59,583
Strength attracts challengers.

163
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,166
-Aah!
-[explosion]

164
00:07:06,166 --> 00:07:08,375
[circuits shorting,
alerts beeping]

165
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,625
The drone will finish him off.

166
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:51,958
-[thudding]
-Aah!

167
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:05,250
Get rid of him!

168
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:13,750
Stop there! No closer!

169
00:08:16,208 --> 00:08:17,125
[roaring]

170
00:08:21,666 --> 00:08:22,666
[grunting]

171
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:29,375
[grunting]

172
00:08:29,375 --> 00:08:30,333
[circuits shorting,
alerts beep]

173
00:09:05,125 --> 00:09:07,625
[Arin yelping,
alerts beeping]

174
00:09:08,791 --> 00:09:09,708
Aah!

175
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:13,500
This is going to hurt!

176
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,375
[exhaling] Ah...

177
00:09:20,375 --> 00:09:21,625
Thank you!

178
00:09:21,625 --> 00:09:23,916
You're from Riyu's tribe,

179
00:09:23,916 --> 00:09:25,458
the Mountain Dragons, right?

180
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:29,291
You want me to go with you?

181
00:09:29,291 --> 00:09:30,208
Sure!

182
00:09:33,541 --> 00:09:36,250
[♪♪♪]

183
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:44,708
Riyu's family!

184
00:09:44,708 --> 00:09:45,750
Hi, everyone!

185
00:09:48,416 --> 00:09:50,125
[tiny roaring]

186
00:09:53,875 --> 00:09:55,208
[squawking happily]

187
00:09:55,208 --> 00:09:58,083
So good to see you again,
Matriarch!

188
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:01,291
The Matriarch
of the Mountain Tribe

189
00:10:01,291 --> 00:10:03,125
welcomes your return,

190
00:10:03,125 --> 00:10:05,083
Arin of the Crossroads.

191
00:10:05,083 --> 00:10:09,541
I am Leaf Blade,
regent for the baby Matriarch.

192
00:10:09,541 --> 00:10:11,833
I speak to outsiders
for Her Majesty

193
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,666
until she comes of age.

194
00:10:13,666 --> 00:10:15,375
I owe you all big-time.

195
00:10:15,375 --> 00:10:18,541
I was about to be a goner
when those dragons saved me.

196
00:10:18,541 --> 00:10:19,583
[Matriarch squeaking]

197
00:10:19,583 --> 00:10:20,916
The Matriarch says

198
00:10:20,916 --> 00:10:22,458
it is the least we could do

199
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:24,166
for a hero like you.

200
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:25,291
"Hero"?

201
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:26,416
Me?

202
00:10:26,416 --> 00:10:27,625
Of course.

203
00:10:27,625 --> 00:10:30,291
You rescued
and befriended Riyu.

204
00:10:30,291 --> 00:10:32,125
You battled
the Claws of Imperium

205
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:34,000
when they came for our tribe,

206
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,125
and you protected
the Baby Matriarch.

207
00:10:37,125 --> 00:10:40,166
Your actions speak
of the person you are.

208
00:10:40,166 --> 00:10:44,083
Well, I mean,
there was a whole team--

209
00:10:44,083 --> 00:10:47,291
[Leaf Blade] The Matriarch
is indebted to you.

210
00:10:47,291 --> 00:10:48,791
Any help you need,

211
00:10:48,791 --> 00:10:51,125
we will provide it, hero.

212
00:10:51,125 --> 00:10:52,208
Oh.

213
00:10:52,208 --> 00:10:54,916
I did get separated
from my teacher.

214
00:10:54,916 --> 00:10:57,708
Oh, no, Master Lloyd is lost?

215
00:10:57,708 --> 00:11:00,125
No, it's a...
different teacher.

216
00:11:00,125 --> 00:11:01,500
You wouldn't know him.

217
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,208
Actually, on second thought,

218
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:06,916
I think I can find him
on my own.

219
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:08,083
[squeaking]

220
00:11:08,083 --> 00:11:10,125
[Leaf Blade]
If your teacher needs rescue,

221
00:11:10,125 --> 00:11:13,500
then I myself will
accompany you on your quest,

222
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:15,958
by our Draconic Majesty's
request.

223
00:11:15,958 --> 00:11:19,333
[awkwardly]
Sure. Yeah. Good.

224
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:20,958
Good...

225
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:25,750
Down there!

226
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,750
I think I see him!

227
00:11:35,833 --> 00:11:37,583
Huh?

228
00:11:39,791 --> 00:11:40,833
[roaring]

229
00:11:40,833 --> 00:11:41,708
[landing]

230
00:11:43,166 --> 00:11:44,291
Fool.

231
00:11:44,291 --> 00:11:46,625
Weird way to say
"Thanks for the rescue."

232
00:11:46,625 --> 00:11:48,791
Why did you bring
this dragon to me?

233
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:51,541
I once hunted these creatures
for Imperium.

234
00:11:51,541 --> 00:11:52,916
You don't think
I don't know that?

235
00:11:52,916 --> 00:11:54,833
But they insisted they help.

236
00:11:54,833 --> 00:11:57,208
If they recognize me--

237
00:11:59,041 --> 00:12:01,125
Leaf Blade,
can we check that out?

238
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:03,291
[Leaf Blade] Of course.

239
00:12:13,583 --> 00:12:14,791
[beeping switch]

240
00:12:14,791 --> 00:12:18,208
Looks like our potential friend
left this behind.

241
00:12:20,166 --> 00:12:21,583
[muttering]
Get rid of the dragon.

242
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,625
Thanks for everything,
Leaf Blade,

243
00:12:24,625 --> 00:12:26,083
but my teacher and I

244
00:12:26,083 --> 00:12:28,791
have to get to the Temple
of the Dragon Cores, and--

245
00:12:28,791 --> 00:12:31,208
The Matriarch
would want me to help you.

246
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,916
I will take you there.

247
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:48,666
It's like watching
a graceful dance.

248
00:12:54,208 --> 00:12:55,625
Are you seeing this?

249
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:57,250
Little busy.

250
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:58,875
If we're gonna fight
Dragonians,

251
00:12:58,875 --> 00:13:00,125
we gotta be able
to fly like them.

252
00:13:06,958 --> 00:13:10,625
I can never operate
at peak efficiency without you.

253
00:13:10,625 --> 00:13:13,750
That is the sweetest thing
you have ever said.

254
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:16,625
Perhaps, once the threat
from the Forbidden Five

255
00:13:16,625 --> 00:13:17,541
is neutralized--

256
00:13:17,541 --> 00:13:19,083
-Yes.
-But...

257
00:13:19,083 --> 00:13:21,208
I did not ask a question yet.

258
00:13:21,208 --> 00:13:22,416
Were you going to ask

259
00:13:22,416 --> 00:13:24,750
if we could explore
the Merged Lands together?

260
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:25,916
Affirmative.

261
00:13:25,916 --> 00:13:28,333
My answer is yes.

262
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:29,958
[beeping]

263
00:13:29,958 --> 00:13:32,500
We have located
the final Prismatic Blade.

264
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,125
[sighing in delight]

265
00:13:46,125 --> 00:13:48,333
They recognized me.

266
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:49,791
[Arin] Don't be paranoid.

267
00:13:59,250 --> 00:14:00,666
[Leaf Blade]
I will wait for you.

268
00:14:00,666 --> 00:14:03,250
You don't have to do that.

269
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:04,416
I insist.

270
00:14:04,416 --> 00:14:06,958
Okay, then.

271
00:14:09,458 --> 00:14:11,416
All right, Janus Melons...

272
00:14:11,416 --> 00:14:12,791
[revving engine]

273
00:14:12,791 --> 00:14:14,583
...get ready for the getting.

274
00:14:17,458 --> 00:14:18,708
Whoo-hoo!

275
00:14:30,125 --> 00:14:31,166
Whoa!

276
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:38,208
[grunting with effort]

277
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:53,583
[revving engine]

278
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,916
Ha! Impend this destruction.

279
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,875
Hmm.

280
00:15:13,875 --> 00:15:17,000
I suppose your old teacher
told you who that is?

281
00:15:19,875 --> 00:15:23,291
Lloyd's grandpa,
the First Spinjitzu Master.

282
00:15:23,291 --> 00:15:27,333
People say he created Ninjago,
and some of the other realms.

283
00:15:27,333 --> 00:15:30,791
He did, but he's long gone now.

284
00:15:30,791 --> 00:15:31,791
[grunting with effort]

285
00:15:31,791 --> 00:15:32,833
[smashing]

286
00:15:35,083 --> 00:15:38,875
[stone crumbling]

287
00:15:38,875 --> 00:15:41,250
What-what did you do that for?

288
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:42,875
Spirit of the Temple!

289
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:44,041
Face me!

290
00:15:49,625 --> 00:15:51,708
[Spirit of the Temple]
Welcome, travelers.

291
00:15:51,708 --> 00:15:54,250
I... The statue!

292
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:55,458
Spirit,

293
00:15:55,458 --> 00:15:58,833
is there a way to create
Source Dragon Icons

294
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:01,416
without gathering
Elemental Powers?

295
00:16:01,416 --> 00:16:03,666
There is,

296
00:16:03,666 --> 00:16:05,750
but that knowledge is reserved

297
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:08,500
for descendants
of the First Spinjitzu Master.

298
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,375
I have this.

299
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:15,041
A Source Dragon Icon?

300
00:16:15,041 --> 00:16:16,708
Impressive.

301
00:16:16,708 --> 00:16:19,791
Almost as powerful
as a Dragon Core.

302
00:16:19,791 --> 00:16:21,083
Exactly.

303
00:16:21,958 --> 00:16:23,000
[roaring]

304
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,583
Tell me what I need to know!

305
00:16:25,583 --> 00:16:28,833
[groaning in pain]
Oh, please, no!

306
00:16:28,833 --> 00:16:30,083
[gasping]

307
00:16:30,083 --> 00:16:31,750
Ras, stop!

308
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:34,166
You're hurting him!
-[grunting]

309
00:16:34,166 --> 00:16:35,458
Tell me!

310
00:16:35,458 --> 00:16:36,916
[groaning in pain]

311
00:16:36,916 --> 00:16:40,416
In the depths of the Underworld,

312
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:42,500
the Casket of Bones...
[groaning]

313
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,875
Forge of the Forgotten!

314
00:16:44,875 --> 00:16:46,000
[shouting in pain]

315
00:16:48,208 --> 00:16:50,833
Most helpful. You may go.

316
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:54,458
Fie! A pox upon you villains!

317
00:16:54,458 --> 00:16:55,458
[Arin] I'm not a--

318
00:16:58,708 --> 00:17:01,958
Why do you care what name
that spirit calls you?

319
00:17:01,958 --> 00:17:04,750
Villains hurt people.

320
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:06,291
I don't want to hurt anyone.

321
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:08,041
Will you do what it takes

322
00:17:08,041 --> 00:17:09,791
to get your parents back?

323
00:17:11,875 --> 00:17:12,791
[sadly] Of course.

324
00:17:20,041 --> 00:17:21,083
[Leaf Blade] There he is!

325
00:17:21,083 --> 00:17:22,166
Is it truly him?

326
00:17:23,291 --> 00:17:25,291
You were foolish
to come among us,

327
00:17:25,291 --> 00:17:26,750
Ras of Imperium.

328
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:29,541
Did you think your crime
would be forgotten?

329
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,333
Beware, Arin!

330
00:17:32,333 --> 00:17:34,333
The person masquerading
as your teacher

331
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:36,625
was the leader
of the Claws of the Imperium!

332
00:17:36,625 --> 00:17:39,250
I know. I... I can explain.

333
00:17:39,250 --> 00:17:41,583
[shocked] You knew?

334
00:17:41,583 --> 00:17:43,708
But his soldiers hunted us!

335
00:17:43,708 --> 00:17:45,708
They caged Riyu!

336
00:17:45,708 --> 00:17:48,375
Yeah, but it's... complicated.

337
00:17:48,375 --> 00:17:50,458
No, it is simple.

338
00:17:50,458 --> 00:17:52,791
We will take him
before the Matriarch,

339
00:17:52,791 --> 00:17:53,958
where he will be judged

340
00:17:53,958 --> 00:17:56,333
for his crimes
against Dragon-kind.

341
00:17:57,250 --> 00:17:58,708
[Ras growling]

342
00:17:58,708 --> 00:18:00,583
This doesn't
have to be a fight.

343
00:18:00,583 --> 00:18:03,208
You defend this wretch?

344
00:18:03,208 --> 00:18:07,125
What happened to you,
Arin of the Crossroads?

345
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:09,625
You have every right
to be angry at Ras,

346
00:18:09,625 --> 00:18:11,125
to have a need for justice,

347
00:18:11,125 --> 00:18:13,083
but I have a need too.

348
00:18:13,083 --> 00:18:15,250
I lost my family in the Merge.

349
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:17,541
I've sacrificed
everything else in my life

350
00:18:17,541 --> 00:18:18,541
to find them.

351
00:18:18,541 --> 00:18:19,916
I need Ras

352
00:18:19,916 --> 00:18:22,125
if I have any hope
of getting them back.

353
00:18:22,125 --> 00:18:23,875
You say you're indebted to me?

354
00:18:23,875 --> 00:18:25,583
Then let Ras go.

355
00:18:25,583 --> 00:18:27,000
I'm begging you.

356
00:18:33,291 --> 00:18:34,208
No.

357
00:18:34,208 --> 00:18:36,458
It is too much to ask.

358
00:18:36,458 --> 00:18:38,583
We are taking Ras with us.

359
00:18:40,041 --> 00:18:41,041
[Ras growling]

360
00:18:41,041 --> 00:18:41,958
[roaring]

361
00:18:44,583 --> 00:18:48,000
I'm sorry,
Arin of the Crossroads.

362
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,333
So am I.

363
00:18:57,041 --> 00:18:58,500
Running is needless.

364
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,083
I can destroy them!

365
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:01,666
That's what I'm afraid of.

366
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:08,166
I think we lost them.

367
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,083
They have a tactical advantage
in the skies.

368
00:19:24,083 --> 00:19:25,791
We must stand and fight.

369
00:19:25,791 --> 00:19:27,375
Not happening.

370
00:19:32,625 --> 00:19:33,625
[distant roaring]

371
00:19:33,625 --> 00:19:34,875
There's something I learned

372
00:19:34,875 --> 00:19:36,208
from being a kid in the streets

373
00:19:36,208 --> 00:19:38,916
that a big guy like you
could never teach me.

374
00:19:38,916 --> 00:19:40,541
What could that possibly be?

375
00:19:41,916 --> 00:19:43,458
How being small...

376
00:19:45,458 --> 00:19:47,166
[slamming]

377
00:19:51,041 --> 00:19:52,500
...can be awesome.

378
00:19:59,791 --> 00:20:00,791
[blasting]

379
00:20:04,916 --> 00:20:06,583
[grunting]

380
00:20:06,583 --> 00:20:08,291
Ridiculous tactics.

381
00:20:08,291 --> 00:20:09,291
[Arin sighs]

382
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:10,666
You're welcome.

383
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:15,833
[Wyldfyre] I've got it!

384
00:20:18,208 --> 00:20:20,166
This stew
is going to do wonders!

385
00:20:23,166 --> 00:20:26,250
Old Roby back in no time!

386
00:20:26,250 --> 00:20:28,541
In no time!

387
00:20:31,125 --> 00:20:34,750
A little extra time, maybe?

388
00:20:36,625 --> 00:20:38,458
No change in his vitals.

389
00:20:38,458 --> 00:20:40,333
How could it not work?

390
00:20:40,333 --> 00:20:42,333
You said my logic was perfect!

391
00:20:42,333 --> 00:20:44,291
[Med Bot] That is not what I--

392
00:20:44,291 --> 00:20:45,750
If this isn't the cure,

393
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,791
w-what is?

394
00:20:47,791 --> 00:20:49,708
For many illnesses,

395
00:20:49,708 --> 00:20:52,375
there simply is no cure.

396
00:20:55,750 --> 00:20:57,083
[growling in frustration]

397
00:20:57,083 --> 00:20:58,208
Ugh!

398
00:20:58,208 --> 00:21:00,250
[roaring]

399
00:21:01,250 --> 00:21:02,166
[sighing sadly]

400
00:21:02,166 --> 00:21:04,166
Oh...

401
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:08,083
This would all be a lot easier

402
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:10,291
if everyone wasn't always
trying to capture you.

403
00:21:10,291 --> 00:21:11,375
[Ras] I told you.

404
00:21:11,375 --> 00:21:12,416
Strength attracts--

405
00:21:12,416 --> 00:21:14,250
[Arin] --challenge, I know.

406
00:21:14,250 --> 00:21:17,416
Not sure we need
extra challenges right now.

407
00:21:17,416 --> 00:21:19,583
Everyone thinks I'm like you,

408
00:21:19,583 --> 00:21:20,750
a villain.

409
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:23,250
The Ninja probably think
the same thing.

410
00:21:23,250 --> 00:21:25,333
Who cares what the Ninja think?

411
00:21:25,333 --> 00:21:27,833
Your need to be liked
is a weakness.

412
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:31,250
Guess it's not like

413
00:21:31,250 --> 00:21:33,250
I'll see any of them
anytime soon.

414
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,708
[vehicle landing nearby]

415
00:21:39,791 --> 00:21:40,916
Arin?

416
00:21:42,291 --> 00:21:43,291
Sora?

417
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

